    Declare token permissions in all workflows (#8178)
    
    Only the ICLA check declared what its GITHUB_TOKEN may do. Every other
    workflow ran with the repository default, which is read and write to
    everything. That is far more than any of them needs: most only read the
    repository, pushes and deployments go through deploy keys or S3, and the
    two workflows handling pull_request_target events from forks could have
    modified anything in the repository.
    
    Declare the minimum for each workflow. Write access remains only where
    the token is actually used to push (npm and submodule updates, release
    tag), to create a release, or to label and comment on pull requests. The
    submodule update keeps write access until #8177 switches it to the
    deploy key; it can then drop to read as well.
    
    Follow-up once this is merged: wait until the workflows which still
    write with the token (npm update, submodule update, release) have each
    run successfully once, then switch the repository default under Settings
    » Actions » General » Workflow permissions to "Read repository contents
    and packages permissions". From then on, the blocks declared here are
    the only source of write access.
    
